course: dictionary
lesson: 7770
title: Pushy and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pushy describes someone who tries too hard to get what they want. A pushy person keeps going, tells others what to do, or pressures them in an annoying way. «Nah, sorry» is a full answer; you don't have to give reasons to a pushy older kid.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Pushy people keep asking, do not take no for an answer, or push in front of others. A pushy salesperson keeps trying to make you buy something even after you have said no.
explain: Pushy is an adjective, so it describes a person. It can get stronger: pushier, then pushiest. A bit pushy means a little too keen to get your own way, and don't be pushy means do not press too hard.
explain: Being pushy is not the same as being confident. Asking once, politely, is fine. Keeping on at someone who has already said no is pushy. If an adult or older child pressures you to do something you feel bad about, that is a time to say no and tell a trusted adult.
fact: Pushy means trying too hard to get what you want, often in an annoying way.
fact: «Pushy» can describe a salesperson who keeps trying to make you buy.
fact: Pushier and pushiest compare how pushy someone is.
fact: «Nah, sorry» is a full answer; you don't have to give reasons to a pushy older kid.
fact: If someone pressures you to do something you feel bad about, say no and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Nah, sorry» is a full answer; you don't have to give reasons to a pushy older kid. What does pushy mean here? | Always lost | *Trying too hard to get their own way | Very hungry | Shy and quiet
exercise: A pushy salesperson keeps asking you to buy after you have said no. What does pushy suggest? | Speaking very softly | Giving you a free gift | *Pressuring you in an annoying way
exercise: Which word means the most pushy? | Pushier | Pushed | Pushes | *Pushiest
test: Someone keeps pressing you to do something you feel bad about. What should you do? | Do it quickly so they will stop | Keep it secret forever | *Say no and tell a trusted adult | Agree, because pushy people are always right
test: What does «a bit pushy» mean? | Always singing | *A little too keen to get your own way | Lost in a crowd | Very polite and gentle
exam: What does the advice «don't be pushy» mean? | Always push to the front of the line | *Do not try too hard to get your own way | Be loud at every party | Ask for everything twice
